description: rasterize Linux notification icons with the profile's ColorProvider
author: Thomas Anderson (Chromium)
origin: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/5802498fae18362e9e90861ae5145054aa0d89c9

Backport of Chromium CL 8791836 (crbug.com/573427860), first released in
160.0.8157.0. The upstream commit also adds a unit test, left out here
because this package builds no tests.

--- a/chrome/browser/notifications/notification_platform_bridge_linux.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/notifications/notification_platform_bridge_linux.cc
@@ -467,7 +467,10 @@
     }
 
     // Prepare resource files.
-    gfx::Image icon(copy_notification->icon().Rasterize(nullptr));
+    // Vector icons (e.g. from ui::ImageModel::FromVectorIcon()) need a
+    // ColorProvider to resolve their color ids.
+    gfx::Image icon(copy_notification->icon().Rasterize(
+        ThemeServiceFactory::GetForProfile(profile)->GetColorProvider()));
     gfx::Image notification_icon = using_portal_
                                        ? ResizeImageToPortalMaxSize(icon)
                                        : ResizeImageToFdoMaxSize(icon);
